                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 3 at 6:47AM ChST until October 5 at 4:00AM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Guam, Rota, Saipan and Tinian.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Sunday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Typhoon Choi-wan (26W) is nearly stationary and is expected to\npivot north-northeast through the northern CNMI through the\nweekend near Pagan and Agrihan. To the south of Choi-wan, surging\nmonsoon inflow will maintain wet conditions into early next week,\nresulting in 4 to 6 inches of rain for Guam and Rota, and 5 to 8\ninches for Tinian and Saipan during the Watch period.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
